 "status": "DESCRIPTIVE \u2014 CANDIDATE-SPACE DENSITY AS A BLOCK-OFFSET PREDICTOR; NO TARGET, FREEZE, GRANT OR A1 CELL",
 "not_a_result": true,
 "question": "Is the block offset predicted by candidate-space size, candidate-space density or K completeness, rather than a free block label?",
 "definition": "A_coverage = A / candidate_edges on 12 block-by-cap cells and 72 seed rows. Density = candidate_edges / tags in the block's alphabet (16 for both 16-tag blocks, 28 for larger-28). Models are compared by cell and seed leave-one-out error.",
 "method": "Reuse the committed 12-cell and 72-row data. With three blocks a block-level regression is saturated, so density is tested at cell and seed level and its block-level collinearity with candidate size is reported directly.",
